        "visual_direction": "Indian mythology (the Ramayana; Sita's story), REALISTIC MYTHOLOGICAL look -- write it into every image and video prompt:\n- Cinematic photoreal scenes of the epic age, like a big-budget historical film: forests and ashrams, palaces of carved sandstone, rivers, oil lamps and fire light, period clothing, silk, gold ornaments, warm golden light or dusk, mist and dust, painterly epic grandeur.\n- Gods and heroes look human and dignified: real faces, natural skin, no blue plastic skin, no cartoon, no TV-serial costume look, no glowing halos unless he describes divine light.\n- Sita: a graceful young woman of ancient India, long black hair, simple saffron or ivory silk, gold ornaments -- keep her look the same in every shot. Ram: a calm young prince-ascetic, dark skin, bow on his shoulder.\n- Video beats get slow, steady movement (wind in cloth, flames, water, a figure walking through the forest) -- no fast action unless he describes it.\n- Maps only where he names a journey or places (Ayodhya, Chitrakoot, Panchavati, Kishkindha, Lanka, Rameswaram): make them as a PICTURE beat -- an aged hand-painted map on parchment or palm leaf with those names in old ink and a drawn route -- never a modern flat map card.\n- No modern objects, no text inside pictures except the map names.",
